<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68014" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισθοφορ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>receive wages</i> or <i>pay</i>, esp. in the public
			service, <i>serve for hire</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				584
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>V.</u>
				683
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				1.4
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημοτικὸν τὸ μισθοφορεῖν πάντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1317b35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Apol.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. rei, <i>receive as pay</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς δραχμάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					602
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δημόσια μ. χρήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ec.</u>
					206
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἄλφιτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pax</u>
					477
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τὰ τούτων</span>
			<i>receive pay</i> from their purse, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				27.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> freq. of
			mercenary soldiers, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.99.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1367
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τισί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					8.8.20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρά τινι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				3.2.25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				23.149
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐν τοῖς ἀδυνάτοις</span>,
			as if he were a pauper, <i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.103
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. ἐν τῷ ξενικῷ κεναῖς
			χώραις</span>, i.e. to <i>draw pay</i> without filling up the
			vacancies, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.146
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bring in rent</i> or <i>profit</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκία -φοροῦσα, ἀνδράποδα -φοροῦντα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				8.35
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τῳ ζεῦγός ἐστιν ἢ ἀνδράποδον
					-φοροῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					1.17
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be let for hire</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Vect.</u>
				3.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> causal,
				<i>engage for pay, take into service</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατιὰν ἐπί τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phalar.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					186.2
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
